	(text "U6 buffers the host bus (A side, PI_3V3) onto the protected bus (B side). The B side and\nits pull-ups run from SAFE_3V3, so EXP_3V3 cannot drive these nodes.\nR40/R41 (1.8 kΩ) with R42/R43 (22 kΩ) hold the idle expansion lines at 3.0-3.1 V (TP18, TP19).\nU10 runs in mode 1 with its local reference: VREF on C19 (TP20), MODE from R21/R22.\nOn over-voltage it opens the expansion lines instead of clamping them into a supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 90.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1474b267-52ca-5fb1-8e9c-bb632240dc23")
	)
	(text "Expansion I2C buffer and over-voltage switch (U6, U10)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27896c45-0632-5a9e-91ec-27724e3c5264")
	)
	(text "U7 is connected the reverse way to U6: host bus on the B side (PI_3V3),\n5 V LED-driver bus on the A side (SYS_5V, R38/R39 1.8 kΩ pull-ups).\nThe LED driver U3 is on sheet 5 (Underlighting)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.35 90.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66d7d0e1-671d-5027-8497-a6a03b3c0376")
	)
	(text "LED-driver I2C buffer (U7)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 256.54 16.51 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "45ae5397-f0ba-5be1-b04f-78a31b10563f")
	)
	(text "U8 open-drain outputs are pulled up through RN3 (1 kΩ) to the switched rails SENSOR_5V and\nSERVO_5V, so a disabled accessory is not back-powered through its signal line.\nR5/R6 (330 Ω) protect the outputs against a 5.5 V fault on the connector.\nU9 Schmitt inputs tolerate 5.5 V; RN3 elements 3 and 4 are 1 kΩ series resistors to the host.\nR44 holds ECHO_INPUT low and R17 holds EXP_INT_INPUT high when nothing drives them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 228.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "33420711-5e9f-50d5-859f-c6bc82f1a465")
	)
	(text "Ultrasonic, servo and interrupt buffers (U8, U9, RN3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cfa32dc7-7035-5322-9e66-1c9ef2203144")
	)
	(text "U30 switches SENSOR_5V from SYS_5V. EN is active high, from the safety MCU U12.\nU30 latches off after an overload; R32 (210 kΩ) sets the limit to 108-154 mA.\nFAULT drives the shared open-drain MOTOR_FAULT bus. R46 discharges SENSOR_5V when off.\nR34 and R33 (2.2 Ω, pulse-rated) damp hot-plug ringing in the returns of C35 and of the\nservo-rail capacitor C32 on sheet 4 (Independent safety supervisor); they carry no DC load current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.28 228.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "640b18ec-980a-52f9-9073-4330b07da73d")
	)
	(text "Sensor 5 V switch and capacitor returns (U30, R33, R34)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8149d203-5bf8-5b9b-b837-9382f40b35bf")
	)
	(text "Notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 254.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4d69579-4e1f-549a-9b43-3a3a5053cdc5")
	)
	(text "1. The ESD clamps of the connector-side lines sit at the connectors, on sheet 9 (Connector-local ESD).\n2. SAFE_3V3 (safety-domain rail), SERVO_5V (switch U15), SENSOR_POWER_EN (MCU U12) and\n   SERVO_CAP_RETURN (C32) come from sheet 4 (Independent safety supervisor).\n3. Expected readings at TP18-TP20 are on sheet 10 (Signal and programming probe access)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 258.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2fed6b06-51d9-5c97-aa6a-a9fe886b35ee")
	)
